---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const identitySchema = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Organization',
  name: 'USD Impact',
  legalName: 'SC Kela Leads SRL',
  url: 'https://usd-impact.com/',
  taxID: 'RO CUI 40790448',
  email: 'support@usd-impact.com',
  founder: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Mircea Albulescu',
  },
});
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About & Transparency | Who Operates USD Impact"
  description="The legal operator, founder identity, model-evidence limits and reproducibility roadmap for USD Impact."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={identitySchema}></script>

  <section class="hero transparency-hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow">About &amp; transparency</div>
      <h1>Who is behind USD Impact?</h1>
      <p class="lead">USD Impact is an early-stage educational macro-finance project operated by a named Romanian company. This page separates verified facts, first-party disclosures and claims that have not been established.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main class="container transparency-page">
    <section class="identity-grid" aria-label="Operator and founder">
      <article class="card identity-card">
        <div class="eyebrow">Legal operator</div>
        <h2>SC Kela Leads SRL</h2>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Jurisdiction</dt><dd>Romania</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Unique identification code</dt><dd>CUI 40790448</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Trade Register number</dt><dd>J38/820/2020</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Contact</dt><dd><a href="mailto:support@usd-impact.com">support@usd-impact.com</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="evidence-note"><strong>Evidence level:</strong> first-party legal disclosure, consistent across the Terms, Privacy Notice and Refund Policy. The identifiers can be checked through the <a href="https://myportal.onrc.ro/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Romanian National Trade Register Office portal</a>.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card identity-card">
        <div class="eyebrow">Founder &amp; authorial lead</div>
        <h2>Mircea Albulescu</h2>
        <p>Mircea Albulescu is the founder and authorial lead behind USD Impact and <em>Read the Dollar First</em>. SC Kela Leads SRL is the accountable service provider and publisher for the project.</p>
        <p class="evidence-note"><strong>Evidence level:</strong> high-confidence first-party identity disclosure. USD Impact has not yet published an independent identity attestation, third-party executive profile or notarized verification, so this should not be represented as independently verified.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="transparency-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">Evidence register</div>
      <h2>Direct answers to due-diligence questions</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Public answer</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Legal entity operating USD Impact</td><td>SC Kela Leads SRL, Romania; CUI 40790448; Trade Register J38/820/2020.</td><td><span class="status disclosed">Disclosed</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Founder / author identity</td><td>Mircea Albulescu, founder and authorial lead.</td><td><span class="status partial">First-party disclosed</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Exact product revenue and customers</td><td>Not publicly disclosed. USD Impact does not use revenue, customer-count or sales claims as social proof. Any future figures should be dated, scoped and separately verified before publication.</td><td><span class="status partial">Private</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Complete historical sales reconstruction</td><td>No independently audited, all-channel historical sales reconstruction is published.</td><td><span class="status gap">Not established</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Independent audited score performance</td><td>No independent model-performance audit has been commissioned or completed.</td><td><span class="status gap">None</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Meaningful predictive power</td><td>Not established and not claimed. Score v2 remains descriptive. A separate preregistered study will test one-week DXY direction prospectively, but no result exists before 52 resolved future predictions.</td><td><span class="status gap">Not established</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Full mathematical methodology</td><td>The variables, signed weights, normalization, clipping, missing-data rules, thresholds and limitations are public.</td><td><a class="status disclosed" href="/score/methodology/">Published</a></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Historical-score revisions</td><td>Yes. Full-sample normalization and provider revisions can change recalculated history. Dated archives preserve what was published, and the revision audit compares each valid archive's latest reading with the same week in the current recalculation.</td><td><a class="status disclosed" href="https://usd-impact-pipeline.pages.dev/data/research/score_v2_vintage_comparison_latest.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Published</a></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Genuine predictive out-of-sample test</td><td><a href="https://github.com/usdimpact/usd-impact-pipeline/blob/main/research/score_v2_predictive_preregistration.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Preregistered before the holdout</a>, with the first untouched origin on August 28, 2026. It fixes a one-week DXY target, 52 resolved predictions, two comparators and an all-conditions-required success rule. It has not started and has no result.</td><td><span class="status partial">Preregistered; pending</span></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="transparency-section">
      <div class="eyebrow">Reproducibility roadmap</div>
      <h2>What is fixed, and what remains</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap roadmap-table">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Action</th><th>Current status</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>High</td><td>Publish as-published versus recalculated historical vintages</td><td><a href="https://usd-impact-pipeline.pages.dev/data/research/score_v2_vintage_comparison_latest.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Published in JSON</a> and <a href="https://usd-impact-pipeline.pages.dev/data/research/score_v2_vintage_comparison_latest.csv" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CSV</a>. Valid archived readings are compared with current recalculations; invalid legacy archives are explicitly reported and excluded rather than rewritten.</td><td>Prevents hindsight ambiguity.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>High</td><td>Specify fields, futures rolls, holidays and timestamps</td><td><a href="https://usd-impact-pipeline.pages.dev/data/score_v2_data_semantics.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Published as a machine-readable contract</a>.</td><td>Defines the exact replication boundary.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>High</td><td>Archive raw inputs and calculation outputs</td><td><a href="https://usd-impact-pipeline.pages.dev/data/score_v2_data_semantics.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Strengthened for strict releases from August 28, 2026</a>: one same-run provider snapshot feeds the score and reproduction bundle. The release week's levels and calculation moments are frozen alongside per-driver and complete-matrix SHA-256 fingerprints for both provider-derived daily histories before forward fill and the complete weekly matrix. Complete raw provider responses remain unarchived and are not publicly redistributed; the conservative boundary is documented in the <a href="https://github.com/usdimpact/usd-impact-pipeline/blob/main/docs/source-retention-policy.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">source-retention policy</a>.</td><td>Detects later daily or weekly input-history changes while respecting data-provider boundaries.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>High</td><td>Run a genuine predictive out-of-sample study</td><td><a href="https://github.com/usdimpact/usd-impact-pipeline/blob/main/research/score_v2_predictive_preregistration.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Protocol preregistered</a> and <a href="https://github.com/usdimpact/usd-impact-pipeline/blob/main/research/score_v2_predictive_engine_lock.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">collector/evaluator locked before the first origin</a>. Weekly evidence PRs cannot merge themselves. The formal result requires 52 consecutive resolved predictions and is expected no earlier than August 27, 2027 if no week is missed.</td><td>Tests the narrow predictive claim without hindsight or backfill.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Medium</td><td>Component and leave-one-out diagnostics</td><td>Published in the robustness research.</td><td>Reveals concentration and dependence.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Medium</td><td>Sign-sensitivity analysis</td><td>Published in the current robustness research.</td><td>Tests directional assumptions.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Medium</td><td>Score-distribution and regime-duration charts</td><td>Research summaries are published; charts are implemented for the next generated weekly dashboard.</td><td>Shows how the indicator behaves in practice.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Low</td><td>Add alternative data vendors</td><td>Not implemented; equivalence criteria are documented before any source change.</td><td>Improves long-term resilience.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bottom-line card">
      <div class="eyebrow">Bottom line</div>
      <h2>Transparent, reproducible and deliberately limited.</h2>
      <p>USD Impact can make a credible claim to a public formula, visible revision policy, dated publication archive, expanding robustness evidence and a predictive study registered before its holdout. It cannot yet make a credible claim to independently audited performance, predictive power or a completed predictive out-of-sample result. Those boundaries are part of the project record, not footnotes.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .transparency-hero { padding-bottom: 64px; }
  .narrow { max-width: 920px; }
  .transparency-page { max-width: 1100px; }
  .identity-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 24px; margin-top: -24px; }
  .identity-card { border-top: 5px solid var(--gold); }
  .identity-card h2, .transparency-section h2, .bottom-line h2 { margin: 7px 0 14px; }
  dl { margin: 20px 0; }
  dl div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, .8fr) 1.2fr; gap: 12px; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e4e8ed; }
  dt { color: #5a6472; }
  dd { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }
  .evidence-note { color: #4f5c6c; font-size: .94rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .transparency-section { margin-top: 64px; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid #dce2e9; border-radius: 16px; background: #fff; }
  table { width: 100%; min-width: 860px; border-collapse: collapse; }
  th, td { padding: 15px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e6eaef; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { color: var(--navy); background: #f5f7f9; }
  tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .status { display: inline-block; padding: 4px 9px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; text-decoration: none; }
  .status.disclosed { background: #e5f4eb; color: #225e38; }
  .status.partial { background: #fff1c8; color: #715313; }
  .status.gap { background: #f6e4e4; color: #7b2d2d; }
  .roadmap-table table { min-width: 980px; }
  .bottom-line { margin: 64px 0 20px; border-left: 5px solid var(--gold); }
  .bottom-line p { max-width: 86ch; margin-bottom: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .identity-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .identity-grid { margin-top: 0; }
    dl div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 3px; }
  }
</style>
